From 7fb9cec977e636c7df35b26588b493c05a1f102f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Project <noreply@invalid>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 18:05:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 160/160] cpu: add closed arm64 CPU-up admission hooks

Add weak public and internal CPU-up admission hooks to the generic hotplug
path, and dispatch optional callbacks through arm64 CPU operations. Public
checks precede CPU-map work; internal checks cover direct thaw and SMT
paths before CPUHP locking or callbacks.

Wire MT6797 CPU8 and CPU9 to leaf-only CLOSED-owner validation. The hooks
never start a transaction or return success for an A72 target, while CPU0
through CPU7 and methods without callbacks retain existing behavior.
Keep the existing MT6797 boot and disable vetoes unchanged.

Extend the default-off KUnit suite to prove callback routing and complete
owner/P30 non-mutation. This experiment-only change has no certifying
sign-off and is not submission-ready.
